WEBVTT

1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,441
Identity and privilege are central to system hardening.

2
00:00:03,441 --> 00:00:13,118
A system can have strong patching and logging but still be risky if too many users have local administrator rights or if service accounts have broad permissions.

3
00:00:13,118 --> 00:00:22,078
Least privilege means users, administrators, services, and applications receive the access they need for their role, not broad access by default.

4
00:00:22,078 --> 00:00:25,590
Standard user access should be the normal starting point.

5
00:00:25,590 --> 00:00:30,250
Administrative access should be rare, justified, monitored, and reviewed.

6
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:40,213
Local administrator groups, privileged domain groups, cloud roles, endpoint management roles, and remote administration permissions should have clear owners.

7
00:00:40,213 --> 00:00:46,450
Shared administrator accounts should be avoided where possible because they weaken accountability.

8
00:00:46,450 --> 00:00:52,542
Where shared or break-glass access is unavoidable, it needs stronger controls and careful logging.

9
00:00:52,542 --> 00:00:55,195
Service accounts need the same discipline.

10
00:00:55,195 --> 00:01:02,219
Each service account should have an owner, purpose, scope, credential rotation expectation, and review schedule.

11
00:01:02,219 --> 00:01:07,811
A forgotten service account can retain powerful access long after the application changes.

12
00:01:07,811 --> 00:01:11,036
Do not treat service accounts as invisible plumbing.

13
00:01:11,036 --> 00:01:15,624
They are identities with permissions, and their risk should be understood.

14
00:01:15,624 --> 00:01:18,061
Emergency access is part of resilience.

15
00:01:18,061 --> 00:01:25,731
During an outage, administrators may need protected ways to recover systems even when normal identity services are impaired.

16
00:01:25,731 --> 00:01:29,673
Those procedures should be documented, tested, and restricted.

17
00:01:29,673 --> 00:01:41,214
Good privilege management balances protection and recovery: administrative power is limited and observable, but authorized teams can still restore service safely when something breaks.
